    "version": "architectural-plan-1",
    "id": "saint-lucia-waterfront-estate-01",
    "thesis": "A low, shaded waterfront estate organized as a limestone-and-timber promenade: a memorable south arrival court leads through a compressed entry sequence into a broad north-facing living terrace, pool, and conceptual ocean outlook. A three-suite guest wing forms a private western garden edge, while a compact upper retreat holds three further suites above the arrival-side stair volume. Deep bronze roof planes, timber screens, and recessed openings give the facade climatic depth without treating the waterfront elevation as uniformly glazed.",
